# Environment configuration for the DeRec reference app.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. Every line is optional; commented-out values show the
# built-in default. Three ways this file is read:
#
#   * by compose, as `env_file: .env` — its DEREC_* variables are passed into
#     the container;
#   * by compose, to substitute `${LAN_IP}` and the port variables in
#     compose.yaml and examples/compose.*.yaml — only when this
#     `.env` sits at the project directory (the repo root);
#   * by the server itself, from its working directory (apps/backend/ for
#     `cargo run`) — and then it fills only variables that are NOT already set,
#     so a real environment variable always wins.
#
# Any of these outranks the config file. An empty value counts as unset.

# This machine's LAN address. Read by compose only, to build DEREC_BASE_URL in
# the compose files, whose `environment:` entry wins over a DEREC_BASE_URL set
# below. ./start.sh --lan sets it for you.
# LAN_IP=192.168.0.28

# Host ports the compose files publish, and tell the node to advertise. Change
# these rather than the mappings themselves (macOS's AirPlay Receiver holds
# 5000, for one). Read by compose only; ./start.sh picks free ones by itself.
# DEREC_HOST_PORT=5000
# DEREC_HOST_GRPC_PORT=50051

# Peers post back to this address, so loopback works right up until a second
# device joins. No port — the node appends its own. Under compose, set LAN_IP
# above instead.
# DEREC_BASE_URL=http://localhost

# The HTTP listener port INSIDE the container (or of `cargo run`). Under compose
# this is coupled to the right-hand side of `ports:` — change one without the
# other and the mapping points at nothing. To publish on another host port,
# change only the left-hand side of the mapping and set DEREC_PUBLIC_PORT.
# DEREC_PORT=5000
# DEREC_PUBLIC_PORT=5000

# Where state lives. A bare path is SQLite; anything with :// is passed through
# untouched. Unset, it is "derec.db" in the working directory for `cargo run`,
# and /var/lib/derec/derec.db in the image, on the volume that makes it durable.
# DEREC_DATABASE_URL=./derec.db

# A scratch node that forgets everything on exit:
# DEREC_DATABASE_URL=sqlite::memory:

# Built front-end assets to serve. Unset serves no UI under `cargo run`, which
# is right beside a Vite dev server; the image serves /app/static.
# DEREC_STATIC_DIR=/app/static

# Where to read the config file from. Unset: config.toml in the working
# directory, or /etc/derec/config.toml in the image. A path named here that does
# not exist aborts the boot.
# DEREC_CONFIG_PATH=/etc/derec/config.toml

# Image only: the directory the entrypoint hands to the runtime user (uid
# 10001) before starting. Set it when the database is on a bind mount other
# than /var/lib/derec.
# DEREC_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/derec

# A smaller set than the default 7, for a quicker loop. The count is usually
# all you need: the thresholds and the transport breakdown adapt to it unless
# you pin them. Pin one only on purpose — a pinned value must stay consistent
# with the count, and that check runs on the MERGED result of file and env.
# DEREC_PARTICIPANT_COUNT=3
# DEREC_PRE_PAIRED_COUNT=1
# DEREC_MIN_PARTICIPANTS=2
# DEREC_RECOMMENDED_PARTICIPANTS=2
# DEREC_HELPER_TRANSPORTS_HTTP=3
# DEREC_HELPER_TRANSPORTS_GRPC=0
# DEREC_HELPER_TRANSPORTS_BOTH=0
